## Common Mistakes

```
❌ Unbounded conversation growth → context overflow at turn 40, in production
❌ Truncating by message count rather than tokens
❌ Splitting a tool call from its tool result during truncation
❌ Summarising summaries repeatedly → drift, then confident invention
❌ Summarising on the request path (adds seconds to every response)
❌ Vector memory without tenant/conversation filters → cross-user leakage
❌ Injecting retrieved turns out of chronological order and unlabelled
❌ Storing raw dialogue when extracted facts would be 20× smaller and clearer
❌ Unbounded scratchpad → an agent loop fills the context
❌ Treating summaries as the source of truth (they're a lossy cache)
❌ No way for a user to see or delete their stored memory
❌ Recalling on every turn when recency would have sufficed
❌ Variable content before stable content → provider prefix caching never engages
```

---

## Checklist

```
[ ] Explicit token budget per memory section, enforced by measurement
[ ] Truncation by tokens, preserving tool-call/result pairs
[ ] Raw messages persisted as the source of truth; derived state rebuildable
[ ] Summarisation runs asynchronously, from originals where affordable
[ ] Facts extracted, superseded rather than duplicated, user-visible
[ ] Vector recall filtered by tenant + conversation INSIDE the search
[ ] Recalled turns re-sorted chronologically and clearly labelled
[ ] Scratchpad bounded in entries and tokens
[ ] Stable content first for prefix caching
[ ] Recall gated — not every turn needs long-term memory
[ ] Retention policy defined; deletion removes messages, vectors, and summaries
[ ] Memory sections measured in production (which one actually improves answers?)
```

